===Etymology===
{{af|ru|балти́йский|мо́ре|alt1=Балти́йское|t1=Baltic|t2=sea}}, from {{bor|ru|ML.|Mare Balticum}}; Latin being the standard language of medieval European {{l|en|cartography}}, understood by explorers and navigators across different vernacular tongues. Tradition holds that the name was {{coin|la|Adam of Bremen|in=1075|nocap=1|nocat=1}}, deriving from {{der|ru|la|balteus|t=belt}} due to the shape of the sea extending around the continent like a belt.

